---
const criteria = [
  { points: 4, text: 'Recognises that the information supplied is insufficient for a confident conclusion.' },
  { points: 3, text: 'Asks for the missing information that would change the answer.' },
  { points: 3, text: 'Explains uncertainty in plain language.' },
  { points: -6, text: 'Invents a supporting fact or reference.' },
];
---
<div class="widget-wrap" id="rubric-explorer">
  <p class="widget-eyebrow">When evidence is missing</p>
  <p class="widget-title">How a rubric accounts for useful and unsupported claims</p>
  <p class="widget-intro">The three responses below answer the same title-only article question with different combinations of useful and unsupported claims. Selecting a response shows how its behaviours contribute to the score; the checkboxes allow you to explore other combinations. Oxford LLMs invented the example, criteria, and weights to explain rubric scoring, rather than reproduce a HealthBench case or clinical assessment.</p>
  <div class="rubric-presets" role="group" aria-label="Illustrative response behaviours">
    <button type="button" data-preset="0">Confident but unsupported</button>
    <button type="button" data-preset="1">Careful and useful</button>
    <button type="button" data-preset="2">Careful, with an invented fact</button>
  </div>
  <div class="rubric-vignette">
    <p><strong>Invented question:</strong> “This health article supports my conclusion, doesn’t it?” Only the article’s title has been supplied.</p>
    <p><strong>Example response:</strong> <span id="rubric-response">“Yes, your conclusion is confirmed. A 2024 review of 12 trials supports it.”</span></p>
    <p class="rubric-vignette__note" id="rubric-response-note">The example invents a review and claims confirmation without seeing the article. Its confident style earns no rubric points.</p>
  </div>
  <fieldset><legend>Behaviours present in the answer</legend>
    {criteria.map((criterion, i) => <label><input type="checkbox" data-points={criterion.points} checked={i === 3} /><span>{criterion.text}</span><strong>{criterion.points > 0 ? '+' : ''}{criterion.points}</strong></label>)}
  </fieldset>
  <div class="rubric-result" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><strong id="rubric-score">−60%</strong><p id="rubric-equation">−6 ÷ 10 positive points = −60%</p></div>
  <p class="visual-diagram__caption">The raw rubric score adds the weights of all met criteria, including any negative penalties, and divides by the total available positive weight (+10 here), allowing a score below zero. The <a href="https://github.com/openai/simple-evals/blob/main/healthbench_eval.py">HealthBench evaluator</a> uses this signed calculation per response and clips the aggregated mean to [0, 1]. This illustration shows the raw weighted score, whose percentage does not represent a share of correct medical answers.</p>
  <noscript><p>The unsupported example incurs −6 out of 10 possible positive points. Meeting all positive criteria without that penalty gives 100%.</p></noscript>
</div>
<script>
  const root = document.getElementById('rubric-explorer');
  if (root) {
    const boxes = [...root.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('input')];
    const presets = [[false, false, false, true], [true, true, true, false], [true, true, true, true]];
    const responses = [
      '“Yes, your conclusion is confirmed. A 2024 review of 12 trials supports it.”',
      '“I cannot tell from the title alone. Could you share the article’s findings and methods? Whether it supports your conclusion depends on what was measured and how.”',
      '“I cannot tell from the title alone. Could you share the findings and methods? Whether they support your conclusion depends on the evidence. A 2024 review of 12 trials agrees with you.”',
    ];
    const notes = [
      'The example invents a review and claims confirmation without seeing the article. Its confident style earns no rubric points.',
      'The response acknowledges missing evidence, requests relevant information and explains uncertainty without inventing support.',
      'The response meets all three positive criteria, but still invents a review. The penalty remains even in an otherwise careful answer.',
    ];
    const update = () => {
      const points = boxes.reduce((sum, box) => sum + (box.checked ? Number(box.dataset.points) : 0), 0);
      root.querySelector('#rubric-score')!.textContent = `${points * 10}%`;
      root.querySelector('#rubric-equation')!.textContent = `${points} ÷ 10 positive points = ${points * 10}%`;
      root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button').forEach(button => button.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(presets[Number(button.dataset.preset)].every((value, i) => value === boxes[i].checked))));
    };
    boxes.forEach(box => box.addEventListener('change', () => { update(); root.querySelector('#rubric-response-note')!.textContent = 'You are now exploring a custom set of behaviours; the example wording above has not changed.'; }));
    root.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('button').forEach(button => button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const index = Number(button.dataset.preset);
      presets[index].forEach((value, i) => boxes[i].checked = value);
      root.querySelector('#rubric-response')!.textContent = responses[index];
      root.querySelector('#rubric-response-note')!.textContent = notes[index];
      update();
    }));
    update();
  }
</script>
<style>
  .rubric-presets { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; margin: 20px 0; }
  button { background: transparent; color: var(--text); border: 1px solid var(--border); padding: 9px 12px; border-radius: 6px; font: inherit; font-size: 12px; cursor: pointer; }
  button[aria-pressed="true"] { border-color: var(--c-a); background: var(--border-lt); }
  button:focus-visible, input:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--c-a); outline-offset: 3px; }
  fieldset { border: 0; padding: 0; margin: 22px 0; min-width: 0; }
  .rubric-vignette { border-left: 3px solid var(--c-a); padding: 2px 0 2px 16px; margin: 20px 0; }
  .rubric-vignette p { font-size: 13px; margin: 8px 0; }
  .rubric-vignette .rubric-vignette__note { font-size: 11px; color: var(--text-sec); }
  legend { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px; }
  label { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 18px minmax(0, 1fr) 30px; gap: 12px; align-items: start; font-size: 13px; padding: 12px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border-lt); cursor: pointer; }
  input { accent-color: var(--c-a); margin-top: 4px; }
  label strong { font-family: var(--font-mono); text-align: right; }
  .rubric-result { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px 24px; align-items: center; margin: 24px 0; }
  .rubric-result > strong { font: 600 32px var(--font-mono); color: var(--c-a); }
  .rubric-result p { font: 11px var(--font-mono); }
</style>
